the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the calculation date is *a date*; scenario element.
    *a household* is individual or group shall not constitute household.
    the individual or group of *a household* resides in institution; scenario element.
    the individual or group of *a household* resides in boarding house; scenario element.
    the individual or group of *a household* lives with others; scenario element.
    the individual or group of *a household* pays compensation to others for meals; scenario element.

the knowledge base us_statutes_7_2012_m_4 includes:


% 7 U.S.C. 2012(m)(4) — us:statutes/7/2012/m/4
the text of "7 U.S.C. 2012(m)(4)" is at "sources/us/statutes/7/2012/m/4.yaml".

rule individual_or_group_shall_not_constitute_household_1 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2012(m)(4)":
a household is individual or group shall not constitute household if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the individual or group of the household resides in institution.

rule individual_or_group_shall_not_constitute_household_2 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2012(m)(4)":
a household is individual or group shall not constitute household if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the individual or group of the household resides in boarding house.

rule individual_or_group_shall_not_constitute_household_3 with provenance "7 U.S.C. 2012(m)(4)":
a household is individual or group shall not constitute household if
    the calculation date is a date D
    and 2008-10-01 <= D
    and the individual or group of the household lives with others
        and the individual or group of the household pays compensation to others for meals.

